Package: BayGMST
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Reconstruction of Global Mean Surface Temperature
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tyler", "Bagwell", email = "teb6@rice.edu",
           role = "aut"),
    person("Julien", "Emile-Geay", email = "julieneg@usc.edu",
           role = "aut"),
    person("Frederi", "Viens", role = "aut"),
    person("Nick", "McKay", email = "nick@nau.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Fits a Bayesian hierarchical AR(1)-driven state-space model
    relating annual global mean surface temperature (GMST) to a reduced
    paleoclimate proxy (computed from cached or user-specified paleoclimate
    multi-proxy network data), instrumental temperature observations, and
    radiative forcings (greenhouse gases, volcanic aerosols, and solar
    irradiance). Unobserved pre-instrumental temperatures are estimated
    jointly with the model parameters using 'Stan' via the 'instantiate' and
    'cmdstanr' packages. Includes tools to reduce a multi-proxy network to a
    single representative proxy series (via principal component regression,
    partial least squares, LASSO, or supervised PCR), estimate the parameters
    in the reconstruction model, run k-fold cross-validation, provide
    uncertainty quantification on the reconstructed temperatures, and
    visualize reconstructions and posterior draws.
